# SAFETY — What you can believe today

File: guide/Safety.oot
User guide. Canonical URL: https://openooda.org/guide/#Safety.oot

## 1. How to read this page

If a belief would make you less careful, it does not belong here.
Design papers are not guarantees. Those live under /research.

## 2. Packages

Lock lines carry a sha256 and a *declared* cap name.
A foreign ELF does not gain Ooda caps because the lock says `FsRead`.
Ingest pins and wraps. It does not rewrite binaries.

`ooda add --registry` fetches `catalog` and checks minisign
against the pubkey shipped in the CLI. HMAC `index.sig` is not
the public trust path.

Path traversal, extra caps, and yank refuse. Host lookalikes refuse.
`ooda launch --exec` runs only after sha, caps, and yank are ok.

## 3. Install

There is no checksum on the public bootstrap script.
The compiler tree is private. The fetch may 404.

## 4. Research

Security papers under /research are design notes.
Do not quote them as “openOODA does this.”
